[0.45, "o", "Title:      \u001b[1mShip Cargo-Dist Release And Upgrade Path\u001b[0m\r\nStatus:     \u001b[1m\u001b[92mverified\u001b[39m\u001b[0m\r\nArchetype:  \u001b[95m\u001b[1mStrategic\u001b[0m\u001b[39m\r\n\u001b[2m\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1mGoals\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mMG-01\u001b[0m - Ship a Port release contract that publishes cargo-dist archives and installers for Port's supported targets, and expose a `port upgrade` workflow that can consume those release installers or install a locally built revision by tag or git SHA. (\u001b[2mVFdgQWhbn\u001b[0m)\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mChildren\u001b[0m\r\n  Epics (1):\r\n    \u001b[1m\u001b[36mVFdgQWhbn\u001b[39m\u001b[0m - Ship Cargo-Dist Release And Upgrade Path (\u001b[2mdone\u001b[0m)\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mStructural Drift\u001b[0m\r\n  Coefficient: 0.63 (severe)\r\n  Coverage:    entities 302/302 | knowledge 5/43 | source 0/0 | docs 0/17\r\n  Context:     38 knowledge units lack source provenance; 17 project docs are unlinked\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mLatest Log Entry\u001b[0m\r\n    2026-04-02T06:33:42\r\n"]
[1.8, "o", "$ sed -n '1,120p' .keel/missions/VFdgQWXbm/CHARTER.md\r\n"]
[2.25, "o", "# Ship Cargo-Dist Release And Upgrade Path - Charter\r\n\r\nArchetype: Strategic\r\n\r\n## Goals\r\n\r\n| ID | Description | Verification |\r\n|----|-------------|--------------|\r\n| MG-01 | Ship a Port release contract that publishes cargo-dist archives and installers for Port's supported targets, and expose a `port upgrade` workflow that can consume those release installers or install a locally built revision by tag or git SHA. | board: VFdgQWhbn |\r\n\r\n## Constraints\r\n\r\n- Mirror the Keel and Sift cargo-dist release shape closely enough that Port uses the same tag-driven GitHub release flow, installer generation, and release validation vocabulary.\r\n- Preserve Port's actual support matrix. Do not advertise a release target that the current codebase cannot build or operate correctly.\r\n- Keep `port doctor` as the first post-install verification step for shipped binaries.\r\n- Preserve Port's packaged runtime asset resolution so install paths continue to find the bundled docs, scripts, and examples needed by CLI workflows.\r\n\r\n## Halting Rules\r\n\r\n- DO NOT halt while the epic attached to this mission still has unplanned or unfinished work required to ship the release-and-upgrade contract.\r\n- HALT when epic `VFdgQWhbn` is complete, release and installer documentation match the shipped behavior, and the `port upgrade` path is verified with automated evidence.\r\n- YIELD to the human only if the supported release target matrix must change beyond the current Linux and macOS contract, or if an external hosting decision blocks installer publication.\r\n"]
[3.6, "o", "$ keel epic show VFdgQWhbn\r\n"]
[4.05, "o", "Title:     \u001b[1mShip Cargo-Dist Release And Upgrade Path\u001b[0m\r\nStatus:    \u001b[32mdone\u001b[39m\r\nCreated:   \u001b[2m2026-04-02 06:14:44\u001b[0m\r\nStarted:   \u001b[2m2026-04-02 06:19:54\u001b[0m\r\nUpdated:   \u001b[2m2026-04-02 06:33:42\u001b[0m\r\nCompleted: \u001b[2m2026-04-02 06:33:42\u001b[0m (\u001b[2m13m\u001b[0m)\r\nPath:      \u001b[2m/home/alex/workspace/spoke-sh/port/.keel/epics/VFdgQWhbn/README.md\u001b[0m\r\nPRD:       \u001b[2m/home/alex/workspace/spoke-sh/port/.keel/epics/VFdgQWhbn/PRD.md\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1mProblem\u001b[0m\r\n  Port needs the same cargo-dist release contract as Keel and Sift so published installers exist and the CLI can upgrade through one canonical release path.\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mGoals\u001b[0m\r\n  - \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-01\u001b[0m: Publish Port through a tag-driven cargo-dist release flow aligned with Keel and Sift. (A release tag can produce archives and installer artifacts for every supported Port target without manual packaging steps. -> One cargo-dist workflow and config checked into the repo)\r\n  - \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-02\u001b[0m: Give operators a canonical self-upgrade path for Port. (\u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mport upgrade\u001b[0m can install the latest release or a requested git revision through the same installer contract. -> One CLI command with automated coverage for release and source-install flows)\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mScope Drift\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[2m(no scope drift detected)\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mStructural Drift\u001b[0m\r\n  Coefficient: 0.63 (severe)\r\n  Coverage:    entities 302/302 | knowledge 5/43 | source 0/0 | docs 0/17\r\n  Context:     38 knowledge units lack source provenance; 17 project docs are unlinked\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mRequirement Coverage\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[36mFR-01\u001b[39m - Port must define a cargo-dist release configuration and GitHub workflow that publish archives and installer artifacts through the same tag-driven release model used by Keel and Sift.\r\n    Linked goals (1): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-01\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (2): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVFdgVAzQc\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-01\u001b[39m, \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVFdgVAzQc\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-02\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[36mFR-02\u001b[39m - Port must expose a \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mport upgrade\u001b[0m command that installs the latest released CLI through the release installer script when no explicit revision is requested.\r\n    Linked goals (1): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-02\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVFdgVAzQc\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-03\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[36mFR-03\u001b[39m - Port must allow \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mport upgrade\u001b[0m to install a requested git tag or git SHA by reusing a cached checkout, building with a supported local Rust toolchain, and installing the result through the installer contract.\r\n    Linked goals (1): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-02\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVFdgVAzQc\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-04\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[36mFR-04\u001b[39m - Installed Port binaries must continue to locate bundled runtime assets needed by released workflows.\r\n    Linked goals (2): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-01\u001b[0m, \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-02\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVFdgVAzQc\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-05\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[36mNFR-01\u001b[39m - The release configuration and CLI upgrade flow must be verified with automated tests or scripted proof paths that run in the repository.\r\n    Linked goals (2): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-01\u001b[0m, \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-02\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVFdgVAzQc\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-NFR-01\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[36mNFR-02\u001b[39m - Port's release docs, install docs, and CLI help must describe the shipped support matrix accurately.\r\n    Linked goals (2): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-01\u001b[0m, \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-02\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVFdgVAzQc\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-NFR-02\u001b[39m\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mPress Release\u001b[0m\r\n  Status:     \u001b[2mnot authored\u001b[0m\r\n  Guidance:   optional; use for large user-facing value shifts\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mProgress\u001b[0m\r\n  Voyages:              1/1 \u001b[32m\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u001b[39m \u001b[32m1/1\u001b[39m\r\n  Stories:              1/1 \u001b[32m\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u001b[39m \u001b[32m1/1\u001b[39m\r\n  ETA:                  complete\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mVerification Strategy\u001b[0m\r\n  Techniques:\r\n    - Area: Method\r\n    - Installed behavior: Packaged/runtime asset resolution checks from an installed binary layout\r\n    - Release automation: Cargo-dist plan/build validation plus workflow file review\r\n    - Upgrade flow: CLI tests covering release-install and source-build installs\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mVerification Readiness\u001b[0m\r\n  Criteria:              automated 5 | manual 0\r\n  Requirement coverage:  automated 7 | manual 0\r\n  Artifact inventory:    text 0 | media 0 | other 0\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mVoyages\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVFdgVAzQc\u001b[39m\u001b[0m - Mirror Keel And Sift Cargo-Dist Release Contract (\u001b[32mdone\u001b[39m)\r\n"]
